CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-12-15

# ── Debian trixie base image (mambaorg/micromamba): no fixes reachable ──
# The base-image knob (container-base-image in pyproject.toml) is the only
# permitted lever for these system packages, and the current latest micromamba
# digest still ships the vulnerable versions — the fixes are not yet installed
# in any published base layer. Re-eval when micromamba rebuilds against a trixie
# apt state carrying the fix (then bump the digest and drop the entry).

# ncurses: stack-based buffer overflow in infocmp CLI tool (no-dsa, low urgency)
# Our containers never invoke infocmp. Fix only in sid (6.6+).
CVE-2025-69720 exp:2026-08-31

# openssl (libssl3t64, openssl-provider-legacy): unbounded memory growth in the QUIC
# server path -- Initial packets for unknown connection IDs allocate channel objects
# that queue unbounded until SSL_accept() drains them (HIGH). Debian marks it postponed
# ("minor issue, fix along with future update") and deb13u2 is still vulnerable, so no
# fix is reachable. Our containers run no QUIC or TLS server of any kind; openssl is
# linked only for outbound TLS to known NCBI/AWS endpoints via curl/python.
# Re-eval: Debian ships a fixed openssl for trixie.
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-10-31

# acl (libacl1): symlink-traversal local privilege escalation in the acl_*_file()
# functions (HIGH). Fixed only in Debian sid (acl 2.4.0-1); trixie awaits a point
# release, so no base-image digest carries the fix yet. The pipeline never invokes
# the pathname-based libacl APIs, and containers run as root — outside the non-root
# local-attacker threat model. Re-eval: trixie point release / a micromamba rebuild
# that carries it.
CVE-2026-54369 exp:2026-08-31

# ── urllib3 < 2.8.0: via awscli in blast, bowtie2_samtools, kraken2,
# minimap2_samtools; vendored by pip in pysam_biopython ──
# Our awscli usage is `update_blastdb.pl --source aws` in the BLAST container —
# HTTPS to known NCBI/AWS endpoints, no proxy, no attacker-controlled compressed
# streams. No module script invokes awscli in the other three containers, and
# nothing runs pip at run time. Every conda-forge awscli build through 2.38.1 pins
# urllib3<=2.6.3, and pip 26.2.2 (the newest) vendors urllib3 2.7.0, so no pin
# reaches the 2.8.0 fix. Re-eval when the awscli feedstock relaxes the cap and pip
# re-vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0.
# CVE-2026-44431 (HIGH, awscli only): cross-origin header leak in proxied low-level redirects.
CVE-2026-44431 exp:2026-12-15
# CVE-2026-44432 (HIGH, awscli only): decompression-bomb safeguard bypass in streaming reads.
CVE-2026-44432 exp:2026-12-15
# CVE-2026-97687 (HIGH): HTTPS-proxy connections inherit target-server TLS settings such
# as CERT_NONE; needs an HTTPS proxy, and no task configures one.
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2026-12-15
# CVE-2026-97689 (HIGH): unbounded memory in the chunked-response parser; needs a
# malicious server, and the worst case is an out-of-memory task.
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2026-12-15

# ── perl-base (Debian trixie 5.40.1-6): no fixed version available as of 2026-06-04 ──
# The pipeline's only perl invocation is `update_blastdb.pl` in the maintainer-run
# INDEX step (modules/local/downloadBlastDB), which fetches official NCBI/AWS BLAST
# databases via `--source aws`. perl-base is otherwise present only as a Debian
# base-image dependency, not called by any pipeline tool. None of these CVEs is
# reachable on attacker-controlled input in that context. Re-eval: Debian backports
# a fix to trixie perl-base (a rebuild then clears them), or the pipeline gains a
# perl path that processes untrusted tar/regex/glob input.
# Archive::Tar unbounded allocation -> memory-exhaustion DoS (HIGH); trusted tarballs, worst case ephemeral OOM.
CVE-2026-9538 exp:2026-08-31
# Three further perl CVEs surfaced 2026-08-18. trixie is still on 5.40.1-6 and the
# latest published micromamba digest ships that same version, so no fix is reachable
# via the permitted base-image bump. Same exposure as above: the only perl invocation
# is update_blastdb.pl against official NCBI/AWS BLAST databases.
# Perl_study_chunk 16-bit overflow silently miscompiles regexes with >65535 fixed-string
# alternation branches (CRITICAL); no pipeline regex is attacker-supplied or that large.
CVE-2026-13221 exp:2026-10-31
# pack/unpack S_measure_struct integer overflow -> OOB heap read (HIGH); the pipeline
# builds no pack templates from untrusted input.
CVE-2026-57432 exp:2026-10-31
# Storable retrieve_hook_common signed overflow aborts thaw()/retrieve() on a crafted
# SX_HOOK blob (CRITICAL); the pipeline deserializes no Storable data at all.
CVE-2026-57433 exp:2026-10-31

# ── util-linux (Debian trixie 2.41-5): fix exists but is not reachable ──
# libblkid integer overflow in the DOS partition-table parser (libblkid/src/partitions/
# dos.c) reached by probing a crafted disk image or partition table (HIGH). Debian fixed
# it in 2.41.5-0+deb13u1, but the latest published micromamba digest still ships 2.41-5
# and the container Dockerfiles install only `procps` (no `apt upgrade`), so the fix is
# not reachable via the permitted base-image bump. The pipeline never probes block
# devices or parses disk images: util-linux/libblkid are present only as base-layer
# dependencies of mount/login, which nothing in the workflow invokes.
# Re-eval: a micromamba rebuild carrying 2.41.5-0+deb13u1 (bump the digest and drop this).
CVE-2026-53615 exp:2026-10-31

# Same util-linux 2.41-5, same unreachable fix (2.41.5-0+deb13u1): three mount(8) flaws.
# Two TOCTOU races in mount applying post-mount ownership/mode changes and in resolving
# the target path via an ancestor-directory swap, plus a nosuid/noexec bypass through
# LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 (all HIGH). All three require executing mount(8); the pipeline
# never does, and Nextflow/Fusion perform their mounts on the host outside the container.
# mount is SUID root in the base image, so these remain a local privilege-escalation
# surface for an attacker who already has code execution inside a container - defence in
# depth rather than unreachable, which is why the expiry is short.
# Re-eval: a micromamba rebuild carrying 2.41.5-0+deb13u1 (bump the digest and drop these).
CVE-2026-53612 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-53613 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-53614 exp:2026-10-31

# ── pip's vendored dependencies (pysam_biopython) ──
# msgpack out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse after a caught error, and a setuptools
# PackageIndex path traversal (both HIGH). Neither is our dependency: they are reported
# from pip's own vendored bundle at site-packages/pip/_vendor (vendor.txt / bom.cdx.json),
# not from the conda environment, which does not install either package. pip 26.2.2 is
# already the newest release and still vendors msgpack 1.1.2, so no pin can reach it;
# the setuptools entry is SBOM metadata only, with no setuptools code under _vendor at all.
# pip's vendored msgpack is used by cachecontrol to serialise pip's HTTP cache, reached
# only when pip downloads packages -- the pipeline never invokes pip at run time.
# Re-eval: a pip release that re-vendors msgpack >= 1.2.1 (then drop these two).
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-11-30

# ── SQLite FTS5 memory corruption (all containers) ──
# Two HIGH flaws in SQLite's FTS5 full-text extension: an out-of-bounds read in
# fts5LeafSeek() and a heap buffer overflow in fts5ChunkIterate() via an integer
# underflow on a crafted continuation page. Both require executing an FTS5 MATCH
# query against an attacker-supplied database. Nothing in the pipeline opens a
# SQLite database at all -- no Nextflow process, bin/ script or container entrypoint
# uses sqlite3, and the only "db" inputs (taxonomy, viral genomes) are TSV and FASTA.
# libsqlite3-0 is not a dependency of any containers/*.yml; it is base-layer state
# from the micromamba image, which is why all 25 images report it.
# Fixed upstream in SQLite 3.53.2 and in sid (3.53.4-2), but trixie ships
# 3.46.1-7+deb13u1 and marks both <no-dsa> (minor issue), so no yml pin or
# base-digest bump within trixie can reach the fix.
# Re-eval: a micromamba rebuild carrying sqlite3 >= 3.53.2 (then drop these two).
CVE-2026-11822 exp:2026-11-15
CVE-2026-11824 exp:2026-11-15
